// Pixel art as data: one character per pixel, '.' is clear, every other
// character is a palette key. Authored with a scratch generator, then
// committed as plain grids: edit the rows here directly.
//
// Chapter 3-1, Huntington Avenue: the campus at night, red brick and
// limestone, the trolley in the median. Same layout as the rooftop set so
// the chunk baker works unchanged: tiles are 16 x 16, anchor top left, each
// kind one anim whose frames are variants (fps 0, pick by column hash).
// roofTop is the limestone coping over red brick (variant 1 fallen leaves,
// variant 2 a joint with a lamp glint), roofEdgeLeft and roofEdgeRight its
// rounded ends with limestone quoins down the corner, roofFill the brick
// wall (variant 1 a lit window, variant 2 a dark one; weight the plain wall
// heaviest), oneWay a limestone ledge on carved brackets, stone a granite
// block, spikes a broken iron fence top on a granite curb (hazard), brick a
// strapped stack of new bricks on a pallet (breakable), auraBlock the sigma
// crate in a limestone frame, vent a basement window grate in the brick
// (matches roofFill), pipe a steam pipe with a gauge (tileable sideways).
// Bricks that cross a tile edge take their colour from the course only, so
// any variants sit side by side without a seam.
//
// panel: the boarded construction panel a dash smashes (the % tile), 16 x
// 32, anchor bottom left (its bottom on the floor, covering two stacked %
// cells). idle 1 frame; crack 3 frames played once as it breaks (cracks,
// split boards, burst), then draw nothing.
//
// Decor anchor is the bottom left (y is the top of the floor row it stands
// on). Light sources, in decor pixels from the top left: lampPost the
// lantern at (7, 8); stringLights a bulb every 6 px from x 3, hanging 2 px
// under the sagging wire (centre bulbs near row 12); trolleyStop the soffit
// strip, x 12 to 35 on row 5; campusSign the lettering, centre (24, 8);
// goalSteps the doors, centre (16, 26), and two lanterns at (5, 18) and
// (26, 18). campusSign is the breakable L sign here: frame 0 on, frame 1
// flicker (like neonSign). goalSteps (the goal): 4 frames of a slow door
// glow pulse, loop.
//
// TROLLEY: the two-section green and cream trolley, 96 x 40, cab and
// headlights on the right (mirror for dir -1). Rows 0 to 7 are the
// pantograph (its collector bar on row 0 meets the overhead wire); row 8 is
// the roof she stands on. anchor (0, 8) is the vehicle's roof-top-left, the
// point World.vehicles gives as (x, y), so the 32 px body under it fills the
// sim's 6 x 2 tile box.
//
// CAMPUS_GLOW lists the keys that glow: Q lamp, R bulb core, S lit window,
// T dim window, U bright window, V tail light, W spark and phone, X
// headlight, 3 4 the aura sigma, 7 8 warm halos, 9 spark halo, * red halo.
//
// CAMPUS_BACKDROP: three 512 px tileable strips for the parallax, bottom on
// the horizon (the bottom row is solid, so it can be lifted). far (96): Back
// Bay behind the campus, the boxy tower with its lit crown and mast and the
// tall blue glass slab, sodium haze on the horizon. mid (80): the campus
// halls, red and pale brick with limestone bands and lit windows, a columned
// limestone front, a glass block with cold-lit floors and a warm lobby,
// bare trees and path lamps on the lawn. near (64): Huntington Avenue: the
// median with its two rails, catenary poles every 128 px with the sagging
// wire, street trees, cobra-head lamps, a passing car with its head beam.
